cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EntropicEFT: a Lean 4 formalization of Entropic Scalar EFT"
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite the tagged release you built."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chinitz
    given-names: Jake
repository-code: "https://github.com/jakechinitz/Entropic-EFT-Lean"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.8.0
abstract: >-
  A modular Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the finite combinatorial and algebraic
  content of "Entropic Scalar EFT: From Entanglement Microstructure to Gravity and
  Cosmic Structure". Machine-checked results include the 1,680-state boundary ensemble
  and its exact K-squared spectrum, the corrected H.9 closure decomposition, existence
  and uniqueness of the stationary eta*, the gauge factor-split no-go, and joint
  satisfiability of the interpreted premise set in an explicit finite model. Physical
  premises are carried by named structure fields rather than axioms; open completions
  (GFT/CDT embedding, transverse influence functional, strong-field boundary theory,
  arrow-of-time typicality) are interfaces with no global instance.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
  - entropic gravity
  - effective field theory
  - quantum gravity
